---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Stakeholder, Investor & Fundraising Models | Carve Model"
  description="Portable architectural models for stakeholder meetings, investor presentations and fundraising. Explain project ideas, development phases and key features."
  canonicalPath="/stakeholder-investor-fundraising-models"
  ogTitle="Stakeholder, Investor & Fundraising Models | Carve Model"
  ogDescription="Portable architectural models for stakeholder meetings, investor presentations and fundraising. Explain project ideas, development phases and key features."
  active="services"
  imageSlot={true}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={`{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Service","@id":"https://www.physical-model.com/stakeholder-investor-fundraising-models#service","url":"https://www.physical-model.com/stakeholder-investor-fundraising-models","name":"Stakeholder, Investor & Fundraising Models","serviceType":"Architectural models for stakeholder, investor and fundraising presentations","description":"Portable architectural models for stakeholder meetings, investor presentations and fundraising. Explain project ideas, development phases and key features.","provider":{"@id":"https://www.physical-model.com/#organization"},"areaServed":[{"@type":"Country","name":"United States"},{"@type":"Country","name":"Canada"}],"isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.physical-model.com/#website"},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://www.physical-model.com/stakeholder-investor-fundraising-models#breadcrumb"}}`} />
<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={`{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","@id":"https://www.physical-model.com/stakeholder-investor-fundraising-models#breadcrumb","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.physical-model.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Services","item":"https://www.physical-model.com/scale-model-services"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Architectural & Real Estate Models","item":"https://www.physical-model.com/architectural-scale-models"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":4,"name":"Stakeholder, Investor & Fundraising Models","item":"https://www.physical-model.com/stakeholder-investor-fundraising-models"}]}`} />
<style>
.breadcrumb{padding-top:1.6rem;}
.breadcrumb a{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.8rem;letter-spacing:0.04em;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);transition:color var(--dur-2);}
.breadcrumb a:hover{color:var(--cm-text-strong);}
.page-hero{padding-top:1.6rem;padding-bottom:clamp(2.5rem,4vw,4rem);border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.page-hero h1{margin-top:1.4rem;}
.page-hero h1 em{font-style:normal;color:var(--cm-text-muted);}
.page-hero p{margin-top:1.4rem;}
.page-hero__inner{display:grid;grid-template-columns:0.85fr 1.15fr;gap:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,3rem);align-items:center;}
@media(max-width:900px){.page-hero__inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.page-hero__visual{order:-1;max-width:440px;}}
.page-hero__visual{position:relative;}
.page-hero__visual image-slot{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:4/3;border-radius:var(--r-sm);}
.page-hero__visual .corner{position:absolute;width:14px;height:14px;border:1px solid var(--cm-silver);opacity:0.5;z-index:3;}
.page-hero__visual .corner.tl{top:-1px;left:-1px;border-right:0;border-bottom:0;}
.page-hero__visual .corner.br{bottom:-1px;right:-1px;border-left:0;border-top:0;}
.hero__spec{position:absolute;right:-12px;bottom:24px;z-index:4;background:var(--cm-ink-800);border:1px solid var(--cm-border-strong);padding:0.9rem 1.1rem;box-shadow:var(--shadow-lg);}
.hero__spec .tick{display:block;}
.hero__spec strong{font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:var(--w-bold);color:var(--cm-text-strong);font-size:1.15rem;letter-spacing:-0.01em;}
.hero__cta{display:flex;gap:0.9rem;flex-wrap:nowrap;margin-top:1.8rem;}
@media(max-width:560px){.hero__cta{flex-wrap:wrap;}}
.hero__cta .btn--primary,.hero__cta .btn--ghost{background:transparent;color:var(--cm-text-strong);border:1px solid var(--cm-border-strong);}
.hero__cta .btn--primary:hover,.hero__cta .btn--ghost:hover{background:var(--cm-accent);color:var(--cm-accent-contrast);border-color:var(--cm-accent);}
.svc-all-btn{background:transparent;color:var(--cm-text-strong);}
.svc-all-btn:hover{background:var(--cm-accent);color:var(--cm-accent-contrast);border-color:var(--cm-accent);}
.dedi-media{margin-top:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);}
.dedi-media image-slot{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:21/9;}
.dedi-body{padding-block:clamp(3rem,5vw,5rem);}
.dedi-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,4rem);align-items:start;}
.dedi-grid h2{font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.8vw,2.4rem);letter-spacing:-0.02em;}
.dedi-list{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1.4rem 0 0;display:grid;gap:0.8rem;}
.dedi-list li{display:flex;gap:0.7rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:1rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);}
.dedi-list li svg{flex:none;margin-top:4px;color:var(--cm-silver);}
@media(max-width:820px){.dedi-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.svc-section{padding-block:clamp(3rem,5vw,5rem);border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.svc-section h2{font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.8vw,2.4rem);letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin-top:1rem;}
.svc-section .lead-p{margin-top:1.2rem;max-width:68ch;}
.svc-checklist{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1.8rem 0 0;display:grid;gap:0.75rem;max-width:68ch;}
.svc-checklist li{display:flex;gap:0.7rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:1rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);}
.svc-checklist li svg{flex:none;margin-top:4px;color:var(--cm-silver);}
.svc-types{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.6rem);margin-top:2rem;}
.svc-type{padding-top:0;border-top:0;}
.svc-type__media{margin-bottom:0.9rem;}
.svc-type__media image-slot{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:4/3;border-radius:var(--r-sm);}
.svc-type h3{font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:var(--w-semibold);color:var(--cm-text-strong);letter-spacing:-0.01em;}
.svc-type p{margin-top:0.5rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);font-size:0.9rem;max-width:none;}
@media(max-width:760px){.svc-types{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.svc-steps{display:grid;gap:0;margin-top:2rem;max-width:68ch;}
.svc-step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.4rem 1fr;gap:1rem;padding-block:1rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.svc-step:last-child{border-bottom:0;}
.svc-step__n{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);padding-top:0.15rem;}
.svc-step p{color:var(--cm-text-muted);font-size:1rem;}
.svc-note{margin-top:1.4rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);max-width:68ch;}
.formats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1px;background:var(--cm-line-faint);border:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);margin-top:1.8rem;}
.fmt{position:relative;background:var(--cm-ink-900);padding:1.4rem 1rem;text-align:center;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--cm-gray-300);letter-spacing:0.03em;transition:background var(--dur-3),color var(--dur-3);}
.fmt:hover{background:var(--cm-ink-850);color:var(--cm-text-strong);}
@media(max-width:760px){.formats{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);}}
@media(max-width:480px){.formats{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.svc-split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 0.9fr;gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,4rem);align-items:start;}
.svc-split .svc-checklist,.svc-split .lead-p{max-width:none;}
.svc-split__media image-slot{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:4/5;border-radius:var(--r-sm);}
@media(max-width:900px){.svc-split{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.svc-split__media{order:-1;max-width:440px;}}
.svc-split--rev{grid-template-columns:0.9fr 1.1fr;}
.svc-split--rev .svc-split__media{order:-1;}
@media(max-width:900px){.svc-split--rev{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.cs-nav{display:flex;gap:0.5rem;}
.cs-nav__btn{width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--cm-ink-800);border:1px solid var(--cm-border-strong);color:var(--cm-text-strong);font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1;cursor:pointer;transition:background var(--dur-2),color var(--dur-2);}
.cs-nav__btn:hover{background:var(--cm-accent);color:var(--cm-accent-contrast);border-color:var(--cm-accent);}
.cs-scroll{display:flex;gap:clamp(1.2rem,2.5vw,2rem);overflow-x:auto;scroll-snap-type:x mandatory;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;margin-top:1.8rem;padding-bottom:1rem;scrollbar-width:thin;}
.cs-card{flex:0 0 min(92%,560px);scroll-snap-align:start;}
.cs-card__media image-slot{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:4/3;border-radius:var(--r-sm);}
.cs-card h3{margin-top:1.2rem;font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:var(--w-semibold);color:var(--cm-text-strong);letter-spacing:-0.01em;}
.cs-card .svc-checklist{margin-top:0.8rem;}
.svc-faq{max-width:68ch;}
.svc-faq .faq-list{border-top:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);margin-top:1.8rem;}
.svc-faq .faq-item{border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.svc-faq .faq-item p a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;text-decoration-color:var(--cm-border-strong);transition:text-decoration-color var(--dur-2);}
.svc-faq .faq-item p a:hover{text-decoration-color:currentColor;}
.svc-faq .faq-item summary{list-style:none;cursor:pointer;padding:1.3rem 0;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:2rem;align-items:center;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:var(--w-semibold);font-size:1rem;color:var(--cm-text-strong);}
.svc-faq .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none;}
.svc-faq .faq-item .pm{position:relative;width:16px;height:16px;flex:none;}
.svc-faq .faq-item .pm::before,.svc-faq .faq-item .pm::after{content:"";position:absolute;background:var(--cm-silver);transition:transform var(--dur-3);}
.svc-faq .faq-item .pm::before{top:7.5px;left:0;width:16px;height:1.5px;}
.svc-faq .faq-item .pm::after{top:0;left:7.5px;width:1.5px;height:16px;}
.svc-faq .faq-item[open] .pm::after{transform:scaleY(0);}
.svc-faq .faq-item p{margin-top:0;padding:0 0 1.3rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main>
<div class="container breadcrumb"><a href="/architectural-scale-models">← Architectural scale models</a></div>

<section class="page-hero"><div class="container">
  <div class="page-hero__inner">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Services / Architecture &amp; Real Estate</span>
      <h1 class="display-lg measure">Stakeholder,<br><em>Investor &amp;</em><br>Fundraising Models</h1>
      <p class="lead measure">Make the project clear in every meeting.</p>
      <p class="muted measure" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">Carve Model creates portable architectural models for stakeholder discussions, investor presentations and fundraising campaigns. We focus the model on the project idea, development phases and features your audience needs to understand.</p>
      <div class="hero__cta">
        <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact">Get a Preliminary Estimate <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/works">View Our Work <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="page-hero__visual reveal">
      <span class="corner tl"></span><span class="corner br"></span>
      <image-slot id="sif-hero" placeholder="Drop stakeholder/investor model photo" src="/assets/type-masterplan.webp"></image-slot>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Shared reference</span>
  <h2>Give the conversation a shared reference</h2>
  <div class="svc-split svc-split--rev" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
    <div>
      <p class="lead-p muted" style="margin-top:0;">A physical model lets participants examine the project together. It can help explain the overall proposal, show how different elements relate and keep discussions grounded in the same physical representation.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">We begin by identifying:</p>
      <ul class="svc-checklist">
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Who will attend the presentation.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> What they already know about the project.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Which questions the model needs to answer.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> What decision, investment or funding discussion it will support.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="svc-note">Those priorities guide the scale, boundaries and level of detail.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-split__media"><image-slot id="sif-shared" placeholder="Drop a project photo" src="/assets/type-planning.webp"></image-slot></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Project vision</span>
  <h2>Communicate the project vision</h2>
  <div class="svc-split" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
    <div>
      <p class="lead-p muted" style="margin-top:0;">The model should make the central idea understandable without overwhelming the audience.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Depending on the proposal, it can show:</p>
      <ul class="svc-checklist">
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Overall building forms and site organization.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Connections between buildings, circulation and outdoor spaces.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Important amenities, facilities or public areas.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Relationships to surrounding streets and development.</li>
        <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> The features that distinguish the project.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="svc-note">Detail is concentrated where it supports the explanation. Secondary elements can be simplified to keep attention on the main proposal.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-split__media"><image-slot id="sif-vision" placeholder="Drop a project photo" src="/assets/type-concept.webp"></image-slot></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Development phases</span>
  <h2>Explain development phases</h2>
  <div class="svc-split svc-split--rev" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
    <div>
      <p class="lead-p muted" style="margin-top:0;">For projects delivered over time, the model can distinguish existing conditions, initial development and future phases.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Depending on the presentation requirements, we can review approaches such as contrasting finishes, removable sections or separately controlled lighting. The method should make the sequence clear and remain practical for the team presenting it.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Phase boundaries and the information shown at each stage are agreed during scope development.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-split__media"><image-slot id="sif-phases" placeholder="Drop a project photo" src="/assets/type-masterplan-v2.webp"></image-slot></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Audience focus</span>
  <h2>Highlight what matters to your audience</h2>
  <div class="svc-split" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
    <div>
      <p class="lead-p muted" style="margin-top:0;">Different meetings may focus on different aspects of the same project. Investors may need an overview of the development program, while stakeholders or potential donors may need a clearer understanding of particular spaces, facilities or community features.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">We work with you to identify what the model should emphasize and how those elements will be explained during the presentation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-split__media"><image-slot id="sif-audience" placeholder="Drop a project photo" src="/assets/svc-arch-defining.webp"></image-slot></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Portability</span>
  <h2>Built to travel between meetings</h2>
  <div class="svc-split svc-split--rev" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
    <div>
      <p class="lead-p muted" style="margin-top:0;">Portability is part of the design brief.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">We review the model’s dimensions, weight, handling requirements and protective packaging alongside its presentation goals. Tell us whether it needs to be carried by one person, transported in a vehicle or shipped between locations.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Where practical, removable or sectional components can help accommodate transport limits. We also consider the table space and setup time available at each meeting.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-split__media"><image-slot id="sif-travel" placeholder="Drop a project photo" src="/assets/svc-arch-support.webp"></image-slot></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Presentation materials</span>
  <h2>Coordinate the model with presentation materials</h2>
  <div class="svc-split" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
    <div>
      <p class="lead-p muted" style="margin-top:0;">The model can be used alongside drawings, slides, animation or digital displays. Consistent phase names, colors and feature labels can help your team move between the physical model and supporting materials.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Complementary digital deliverables are reviewed and quoted separately when required.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-split__media"><image-slot id="sif-materials" placeholder="Drop a project photo" src="/assets/casestudy-atlanta2-1200.webp"></image-slot></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section" style="border-bottom:0;"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Start with what you have</span>
  <h2>Send us the information you have</h2>
  <div class="formats">
    <div class="fmt">Available plans, renderings or 3D files</div>
    <div class="fmt">The intended audience and purpose of the meetings</div>
    <div class="fmt">Key project features and development phases</div>
    <div class="fmt">Preferred model size and transport requirements</div>
    <div class="fmt">Dates and locations of upcoming presentations</div>
    <div class="fmt">Any supporting materials the model should coordinate with</div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="cta reveal" style="position:relative;text-align:center;background:var(--cm-black);border:1px solid var(--cm-border);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem) var(--gutter);">
    <h2 class="display-md">Start your presentation model.</h2>
    <p class="muted mt-2" style="max-width:52ch;margin-inline:auto;">We will recommend a scope, scale and presentation approach based on the information you need to communicate.</p>
    <div class="hero__cta" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:2.4rem;">
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact">Get a Preliminary Estimate <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/architectural-scale-models">Architectural Model Services <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
